(143747, 7198, 472, '<td valign="top">a lower iso with a longer shutter would have probably been less noisey.  my experience with the dimage cameras is that they tend to be on the higher end of noisy.  with my e10, on the lowest iso, im able to easily do 8 sec exposures with no visible grain.  a lot of canons and sony''s are also pretty good at keeping the noise down .. one more thing you  might want to look into is Neat Image noise reduction software.  Feel free to message me if you want more information.</td>', 'a lower iso with a longer shutter would have probably been less noisey.  my experience with the dimage cameras is that they tend to be on the higher end of noisy.  with my e10, on the lowest iso, im able to easily do 8 sec exposures with no visible grain.  a lot of canons and sony''s are also pretty good at keeping the noise down .. one more thing you  might want to look into is Neat Image noise reduction software.  Feel free to message me if you want more information.', '2002-10-28 08:00:00.000000', NULL, 0),
