(144584, 7274, 3273, '<td valign="top">I hope you didn''t break your camera shooting into the sun like this (and I certainly advise against using a viewfinder if you''ve got one - stick to the LCD).<br/><br/>I like the way that the line from the aircraft goes through the middle of the shot but it might have been better if it could have gone exactly from one corner of the picture to the other.  I never normally think about things like that until after the event though when it''s normally too late (maybe you could have rotated it slightly using software and then cropped it).</td>', 'I hope you didn''t break your camera shooting into the sun like this (and I certainly advise against using a viewfinder if you''ve got one - stick to the LCD).I like the way that the line from the aircraft goes through the middle of the shot but it might have been better if it could have gone exactly from one corner of the picture to the other.  I never normally think about things like that until after the event though when it''s normally too late (maybe you could have rotated it slightly using software and then cropped it).', '2002-10-23 11:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(144585, 7274, 1078, '<td valign="top">I''m one of those who feels this doesn''t fit the challenge since the _only_ light I see in this pic is the sun, and that'' not artificial in my book.  Sorry.</td>', 'I''m one of those who feels this doesn''t fit the challenge since the _only_ light I see in this pic is the sun, and that'' not artificial in my book.  Sorry.', '2002-10-23 12:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
