(144862, 7294, 4106, '<td valign="top">I have no idea what this is or how it relates to the title</td>', 'I have no idea what this is or how it relates to the title', '2002-10-27 21:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(144863, 7294, 4615, '<td valign="top">I deliberately wanted to use lighting to create an atmosphere of mystery replicating a child''s room at twilight.    The cars are first edition hotwheels from the mid-sixties, so they have unorthadox profiles, which apparently threw people off.  Are they cars or spaceships?  The idea of the title is derived from the mysterious appearence toys take on, in the mind of an imaginative child, when the lights go off, hence "while you were sleeping."   Was that really so hard?   <br/>Maybe I should have titled it "Toy cars in the dark" for drfmelanogaster and hedonist et al''s benefit.</td>', 'I deliberately wanted to use lighting to create an atmosphere of mystery replicating a child''s room at twilight.    The cars are first edition hotwheels from the mid-sixties, so they have unorthadox profiles, which apparently threw people off.  Are they cars or spaceships?  The idea of the title is derived from the mysterious appearence toys take on, in the mind of an imaginative child, when the lights go off, hence "while you were sleeping."   Was that really so hard?   Maybe I should have titled it "Toy cars in the dark" for drfmelanogaster and hedonist et al''s benefit.', '2002-10-28 08:24:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(144864, 7295, 3080, '<td valign="top">Quite interesting shot.  Glad you titled it what you did, or I would be even more confused that I am now. LOL.  I mean that in the best way.  My only small nitpick is that the object on the table doesn''t seem to be in focus like the rest of the shot.  was it moving?  Looks the same with the top surface of the table as well, kind of a softer focus than the rest of the photo.  I am interested in finding out how this was done.  Nice one! Good luck in the challenge. ~Hbunch7187~</td>', 'Quite interesting shot.  Glad you titled it what you did, or I would be even more confused that I am now. LOL.  I mean that in the best way.  My only small nitpick is that the object on the table doesn''t seem to be in focus like the rest of the shot.  was it moving?  Looks the same with the top surface of the table as well, kind of a softer focus than the rest of the photo.  I am interested in finding out how this was done.  Nice one! Good luck in the challenge. ~Hbunch7187~', '2002-10-21 03:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
