(492702, 7459, 889, '<td valign="top">Additional comment: It is still the highest rated for this camera type, and I hope to do better in the future.  When I looked back at the orriginal, I didn''t crop it lower down because at that point you can see the water is a muddy color from the street light that was directly over my head. I ended up shielding the lens from that light with my body to prevent the picture from being washed out. Also further left and right there are street lamps that would have looked tacky.<br/> <br/>The fountain was bottom lit by a floodspot that is right in the base of the ''V''.  The fountain was tilted over at a harsh angle.<br/>Edited for typos<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-11-23 13:02:34.</i></td>', 'Additional comment: It is still the highest rated for this camera type, and I hope to do better in the future.  When I looked back at the orriginal, I didn''t crop it lower down because at that point you can see the water is a muddy color from the street light that was directly over my head. I ended up shielding the lens from that light with my body to prevent the picture from being washed out. Also further left and right there are street lamps that would have looked tacky. The fountain was bottom lit by a floodspot that is right in the base of the ''V''.  The fountain was tilted over at a harsh angle.Edited for typos', '2003-11-23 13:01:30.000000', '2003-11-23 13:02:34.000000', 0),
